sment, rehabilitation, and management. Healthcare professionals utilize various diagnostic tests, such as pH-impedance and manometry, to evaluate the severity of the condition. Early detection and treatment are crucial, as untreated DOF can lead to serious health consequences.\n\nThe management of oropharyngeal dysphagia involves not only dietary modifications but also rehabilitation techniques and specific nursing care to ensure safe oral feeding. It is relevant in hospital settings, particularly in food service and preparation, where understanding the dietary needs of affected patients is essential. Additionally, the condition is the focus of various health data collection and management systems, highlighting its significance in clinical practice and research.\n\nOverall, oropharyngeal dysphagia is a complex swallowing disorder that requires comprehensive care strategies to enhance patient outcomes and maintain nutritional health.\",121\r\n41,LOURDES MONEVA VICENTE,\"Lourdes Moneva Vicente is a dedicated nurse in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. She specializes in the nutritional treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia, providing essential nursing care for patients affected by this condition. In addition to her clinical work, Lourdes is also a co-author of a document that emphasizes the importance of oral hygiene, highlighting her commitment to improving patient care and outcomes in her field.\",4\r\n33,MÓNICA BENITO FERNÁNDEZ,\"Mónica Benito Fernández is a dedicated professional in the field of nursing and nutrition, specifically focusing on the nutritional treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia. She is a nurse who graduated in Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics and currently works in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. In her role, she provides nursing care for patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia, ensuring they receive appropriate nutritional support. Additionally, Mónica is a co-author of a document highlighting the importance of oral hygiene, further emphasizing her commitment to patient care and health education. Her research contributions are significant in enhancing the understanding and management of oropharyngeal dysphagia, showcasing her expertise and dedication to improving patient outcomes in this area.\",4\r\n39,CARMEN GÓMEZ TRIGUERO,\"Carmen Gómez Triguero is a Specialist Physician in the Rehabilitation Service at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. She is actively involved in research concerning oropharyngeal dysphagia rehabilitation, contributing as a co-author to various studies in this field. Additionally, she has played a significant role in developing a manual that addresses solutions for oropharyngeal dysphagia, with a particular focus on exercises designed for orofacial structures that are crucial for the swallowing process. Through her work, Carmen Gómez Triguero has established herself as a key contributor to the understanding and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia.\",3\r\n42,NATASHA PÉREZ MARRERO,\"Natasha Pérez Marrero is a Specialist Physician in the Otolaryngology Service at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. She is recognized for her contributions to the clinical guidelines on dysphagia, indicating her expertise in the field of otolaryngology.\",3\r\n101,MANIOBRA DE MENDELSOHN,\"The \"\"MANIOBRA DE MENDELSOHN,\"\" also known as the Mendelsohn maneuver, is a specialized technique designed to enhance the swallowing process. This maneuver focuses on prolonging the elevation of the larynx during swallowing, which serves to improve airway protection and minimize pharyngeal residue. Additionally, it aims to improve the coordination of swallowing and the function of the upper esophageal sphincter (EES). Overall, the Mendelsohn maneuver is an effective strategy for individuals experiencing swallowing difficulties, contributing to safer and more efficient